{:edb/db-before-t 2017 :edb/db-after-t 2018 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535330 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:15:47.434Z" 13194139535330 true] [17592186124403 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344152 13194139535330 true] [17592186124823 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535330 true] [17592186124823 1100 "Consider the set of matrices ${A, B}$, where\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 10\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -12\\end{bmatrix}$.\nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{x_{1}}{x_{2}}$ from a non-zero solution of $x_{1}A + x_{2}B = O$, where $O$ is the $2 \\cdot 2$ zero-matrix." 13194139535330 false] [17592186124823 1100 "Consider the set of matrices ${A,B},$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 10\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B=O,$ where $O$ is the $2\\times 2$ zero-matrix." 13194139535330 true] [17592186124823 1145 "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ not both zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B=O.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the matrices $A$ and $B$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 10\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} & 5{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} & 10{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{2} & 6{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2} & -12{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} & 5{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & 10{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 10{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding augmented matrix and reduce it to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -12 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}/2\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -12 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-10){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. Therefore, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 16{x}_{2}=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich has only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\nConsequently, ${A,B}$ is linearly independent." 13194139535330 true] [17592186344152 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344153 13194139535330 true] [17592186344152 1089 "q-94779" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344152 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535330 true] [17592186344152 1100 "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent\n- ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent\n- ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344152 1113 #uuid "93fea67e-a3d6-502c-9ac5-3b5196ad6f92" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344152 1145 "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}({v}_{1}+{v}_{3})+{x}_{3}{v}_{2} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){v}_{1}+({x}_{1}+{x}_{3}){v}_{2}+{x}_{2}{v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+1\\cdot ({v}_{2}-{v}_{1})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}-{v}_{1})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0$ must have only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$  If this equation has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}=0,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\na\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}+0\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344153 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344154 13194139535330 true] [17592186344153 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344155 13194139535330 true] [17592186344153 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344156 13194139535330 true] [17592186344153 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344157 13194139535330 true] [17592186344153 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344158 13194139535330 true] [17592186344153 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535330 true] [17592186344153 1041 "selection" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344153 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344156 13194139535330 true] [17592186344153 1110 #uuid "1a54f71a-479b-5d56-b285-ef5dc5c6a0eb" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344154 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535330 true] [17592186344154 1111 #uuid "d9c1ab53-475e-5d20-89eb-d0b35c95dbe4" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344155 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535330 true] [17592186344155 1111 #uuid "52183ace-92c7-56bc-8776-c91b11c400f4" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344156 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535330 true] [17592186344156 1111 #uuid "2eaa76a7-fc78-5e34-9000-d521ccc0a082" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344157 1034 "III only" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344157 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535330 true] [17592186344157 1111 #uuid "9535f521-fb4a-5769-9076-2effa2acbb5d" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344158 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535330 true] [17592186344158 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535330 true] [17592186344158 1111 #uuid "9e75fed4-d478-5a86-817d-d77e9e6e93c5" 13194139535330 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-94779" 17592186344152 "q-94779/selection" 17592186344153 "q-94779/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" 17592186344154 "q-94779/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" 17592186344155 "q-94779/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" 17592186344156 "q-94779/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" 17592186344157 "q-94779/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" 17592186344158} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
